ky with oil  and while they did get lucky with their  natural resources that in itself is  nowhere near enough to build such an  Empire and if you don't believe me just  take a look at Venezuela who not only  has more oil than Saudi Arabia but  discovered their oil decades earlier you  would think that such a country would be  filthy rich but there are unfortunately  dirt poor and riddled with  hyperinflation the same thing could be  said about Canada as well who has the  world's third largest oil reserves  Canada is of course by no means doing  bad but given that they've been an  advanced country for far longer than  Saudi Arabia you would think that they  would have been able to capitalize on  their oil way more than Saudi Arabia yet  that's not the case so how did Saudi  Arabia become the winners of the oil  game  foreign  taking a look back Saudi Arabia was by  no means early to the oil game in fact  they were rather late and their entry  into oil wasn't particularly strategic  either it was more of Just A desperate  gamble in the decades preceding Saudi  Arabia searched for oil Saudi Arabia  wasn't even a thing instead the area was  controlled by two families called the  house of sauri and the house of Rashid  who were constantly in Conflict  sometimes the house of Saud would be on  top and other times the house of Rasheed  would be on top but there was really no  winner it was more or less just a big  Power struggle that led nowhere this  however would all change with the turn  of the century in the 1900s at the time  the rashidi family was on top and the  leader of the Saudi family abdulaziz  al-saud was an exile in Kuwait Abdul  hadn't forgotten about the house of  Rashid though and he was simply plotting  his counter-attack which would take  place in 1902 with this initial strike  Abdul would take back Riyadh which was  just the first of a series of of  conquests and before you knew it the  sauds were back in control the rashids  were forced into Exile just like the  sods previously but this was by no means  the end of it the Saudi family knew that  the rashidi family could strike back at  any time just like the sauds did so they  set out on advancing the area so much  that the rashidi family couldn't form a  counter-attack ironically this turned  out to be a non-issue given that the  rashidi family would dissolve in 1921  but the sauds didn't know that at the  time so they started working on creating  an unbeatable Force the first step in  this journey was to actually create an  official country this is what would  eventually lead to the birth of Saudi  Arabia in September of 1932. at this  point they officially had a country but  this didn't mean much without an economy  and unfortunately being surrounded by a  bunch of sand The Sounds didn't exactly  have a bunch of economical options in  fact they really only had it two options  option number one was to leverage their  access to the Sea they could build a  port or go pro diving or fish but this  is what they had already been doing for  Millennia troll diving in the Arabian  Peninsula literally dates back 7 000  years and given their current situation  it clearly wasn't all that profitable  option number two was to leverage their  religious significance Saudi Arabia was  and still is the home to Mecca which is  where millions of Muslims pilgrimage  every year but I suspect that the south  felt that leaning too much into religion  would have threaten their own power I  after all they've been destroying the  city ever since they took over in the  last 37 years or so Saudi Arabia has  demolished 95 percent of Mecca's  historical buildings so clearly becoming  an Islamic Vatican City wasn't a top  consideration with the sea and religion  crossed off as economic options Saudi  Arabia had to think outside the box and  it didn't take them long to take the oil  gamble just one year after the country  was formed Saudi Arabia would sign an  old concession agreement with the 