ch  as they could while they were still in  power this is why a hundred billion  dollars was embezzled by country  officials between 1972 and 1997 alone  and this is also why Venezuelan gold and  currency Reserve stand at just 10  billion dollars while Saudi Arabian  reserves stand at 473 billion dollars  aside from making long-term decisions  and saving up their money Saudi Arabia  also reinvested this money far more  effectively than Venezuela Saudi Arabia  used their money to build businesses  invest into the economy and recruit  International Talent this is why 85 of  Saudi engineers and 18 of Saudi CEOs are  actually expats Vision 2030 is also a  perfect example of this in the meantime  Venezuela was embracing socialism and  spending all of her money on social  programs and subsidizing various  everyday Goods so as Saudi Arabia was  becoming less dependent on oil Venezuela  was becoming more dependent on oil while  this is okay when Oilers strong the same  cannot be said when oil is weak and  that's exactly what happened in 2014  when oil prices crashed and the  Venezuelan economy collapsed while this  crash was not fun for Saudi Arabia  either they were able to comfortably  make it to the other side not because of  any one decision that they made during  the crash but because of Decades of  right decisions  today Saudi Arabia is one of the largest  companies in the world and it's usually  the most profitable now of course these  insane oil prices won't last forever and  that things will eventually cool down  hopefully this means that Saudi aranco's  profits will also cool down with the  time but really all this means for them  is profiting a hundred billion dollars  per year instead of 200 or 300 billion  zooming out to the long term the world  is slowly moving away from oil but this  will probably not impact Saudi Arabia  all that much given that they've been  slowly moving away from oil themselves  and to given that they've been playing  their cards extremely strategically ever  since they found oil I see no reason why  this will change in the coming decades  until then Saudi Arabia will remain as  one of the few countries in which an  authoritarian regime actually worked at  least economically if we're talking  socially that's a whole different story  but that's a topic for another video did  you realize how high Saudi aramco's  profits were common that down below also  drop a like if you hope that all prices  come down sooner rather than later and  of course consider checking out our  Discord Community to suggest future  video ideas and consider subscribing to  see more questions about you answered  but until then I'm Hari and I'll see you  guys on the next one

